<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>Thornfield — Helpdesk built for growing support teams</title>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="tf-hero py-5">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="fw-bold">Support tickets, saved views, and settings — in one place.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Thornfield helps small and mid-sized support teams triage tickets, save the
        filters they check every day, and keep workspace settings in sync with the tools they
        already use.</p>
      <a href="/register" class="btn btn-light btn-lg me-2">Start your workspace</a>
      <a href="/login" class="btn btn-outline-light btn-lg">Sign in</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row g-4">
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="tf-card p-4 h-100">
          <h5>Saved Views</h5>
          <p class="text-muted">Save the ticket filters you run every morning — open tickets
            assigned to you, everything waiting on a customer reply — and re-run them with one
            click instead of rebuilding the search each time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="tf-card p-4 h-100">
          <h5>Settings Import</h5>
          <p class="text-muted">Migrating from another helpdesk? Workspace admins can import a
            settings bundle exported from your previous tool to carry over routing rules and
            notification preferences without re-entering everything by hand.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="tf-card p-4 h-100">
          <h5>Directory Sync</h5>
          <p class="text-muted">Connect Thornfield to your HR or SSO provider so that when someone
            joins, leaves, or changes teams, their Thornfield access updates automatically instead
            of an admin doing it by hand.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
